From 8b1b1df841c9bbca0a8724eb874d8cf22fb51b35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OdissREA <mic.deangelis@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH RFC] arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x: run
 keyboard/touchpad I2C at 100 kHz

On a Yoga Slim 7x (83ED) with BIOS NHCN62WW (12/02/2025) the internal
keyboard (ITE 048D:8987 at 0x3a) never probes and the touchpad (ELAN
04F3:3303 at 0x2c) on the same bus dies a few seconds after boot:

  i2c_hid_of 1-003a: failed to change power setting.
  i2c_hid_of 1-003a: can't add hid device: -110
  i2c_hid_of 1-002c: failed to get a report from device: -110

At 400 kHz the keyboard controller returns a corrupted HID descriptor:
the first 16 bytes are correct, byte 17 is shifted by one bit and the
rest reads back as 0xff:

  1e 00 00 01 b0 00 21 00 24 00 18 00 25 00 40 00 11 ff ff ff ...

Reading the same descriptor slowly (GPIO bit-banging) gives valid data:

  1e 00 00 01 b0 00 21 00 24 00 18 00 25 00 40 00 22 00 23 00
  8d 04 87 89 03 00 00 00 00 00

Because of the corruption i2c-hid uses 0xff11 as wCommandRegister
instead of 0x0022. The SET_POWER write to that bogus register leaves
the controller in the middle of a transfer holding SDA low, which
takes the whole bus (and the touchpad) down until SCL is clocked
manually.

With the bus at 100 kHz both devices probe and work. Lower the bus
frequency.

Signed-off-by: OdissREA <mic.deangelis@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
index a807744..84ee560 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-lenovo-yoga-slim7x.dts
@@ -806,7 +806,7 @@
 };
 
 &i2c0 {
-	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+	clock-frequency = <100000>;
 
 	status = "okay";
 
-- 
